# =============================================================================
# .env.example
# =============================================================================
# PURPOSE: A template for server/.env, which holds the server's secret
# settings. Commit THIS file, but NEVER commit .env (it's in .gitignore).
#
# WHAT TO BUILD: Under the TODOs below, add 4 lines in the form NAME=value,
# without "#" and with no spaces around "=". Leave the values blank in this
# example file, and put the real values in your own .env.
#
# TALKS TO: server.js loads .env with dotenv (process.env.NAME).
#           gemini.js reads GEMINI_API_KEY and GEMINI_MODEL.
#
# STEPS:
#   1. PORT=5000
#        The port Express listens on. client/vite.config.js proxies
#        /api to this port.
#   2. MONGO_URI=
#        Local:  mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/appname
#        Atlas:  mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/appname
#   3. GEMINI_API_KEY=
#        A free key from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey).
#        SERVER ONLY. Never put it in the client.
#   4. GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
#        Switch to a newer Flash model when one is available.
#   5. Copy this file to server/.env and fill in the real values.
#
# CONCEPTS TO LEARN:
#   - Environment variables and process.env
#   - The dotenv package
#   - MongoDB connection strings (local vs Atlas)
# =============================================================================
